 ## Overview
-This method computes the alpha values for all $N$ 2D Gaussians across all $W \times H$ pixels in a single batched operation, serving as the core rasterization step in Gaussian Splatting. It builds on [Single Point Alpha Forward](3478-single-point-alpha-forward.md) by vectorizing the evaluation over the entire image grid, enabling efficient GPU execution. It differs from [Explicit Intersection Alpha Compositing](4814-explicit-intersection-alpha-compositing.md) by computing raw alpha contributions for all pixel-gaussian pairs rather than identifying explicit intersection pairs for compositing.
